1
00:06:36,666 --> 00:06:42,666
Visionary. Billionaire. Fraud?

2
00:13:13,333 --> 00:13:19,333
The Inventor: Out for Blood in Silicon Valley is a
documentary film directed by Alex Gibney.

3
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:56,000
With a magical new invention that promised to revolutionize blood testing, Elizabeth Holmes
became the world’s youngest self-made billionaire, heralded as the next Steve Jobs.

4
00:26:26,666 --> 00:26:32,666
Then, overnight, her 10-billion-dollar company dissolved.

5
00:33:03,333 --> 00:33:09,333
The rise and fall of Theranos is a window into the psychology of fraud.

6
00:39:40,000 --> 00:39:46,000
Self - CEO and Founder of Theranos (archive
footage), played by Elizabeth Holmes.

7
00:46:16,666 --> 00:46:22,666
Self - Narrator / Interviewer, played by Alex Gibney.

8
00:52:53,333 --> 00:52:59,333
Self - Behavioral Economist, played by Dan Ariely.

9
00:59:30,000 --> 00:59:36,000
Self - Fortune, played by Roger Parloff.

10
01:06:06,666 --> 01:06:12,666
Self - The New Yorker, played by Ken Auletta.

11
01:12:43,333 --> 01:12:49,333
Self - Lab Associate, played by Erika Cheung.

12
01:19:20,000 --> 01:19:26,000
The Inventor: Out for Blood in Silicon Valley is a 2019 American
documentary film, directed and produced by Alex Gibney.

13
01:25:56,666 --> 01:26:02,666
The film revolves around Elizabeth Holmes and her former company Theranos.

14
01:32:33,333 --> 01:32:39,333
It is considered a companion piece to the book, Bad Blood:
Secrets and Lies in a Silicon Valley Startup.

15
01:39:10,000 --> 01:39:16,000
The Inventor had its world premiere at the Sundance
Film Festival on January 24, 2019.

16
01:45:46,666 --> 01:45:52,666
It was produced by HBO Documentary Films and Jigsaw Productions with a television
premiere on March 18, 2019, on HBO as well as its streaming platforms.

17
01:52:23,333 --> 01:52:29,333
The film explores themes of technology, fraud, business,
medical research, health documentary.
